      en: "Tadjourah, known as the 'White City,' is one of the oldest settlements in Djibouti, situated on the northern shore of the Gulf of Tadjourah. It has a rich history as an ancient center of the salt trade and a vital port for caravans transporting goods from the interior to the coast. The town is recognizable by its traditional white-painted buildings, which help reflect the intense heat of the region. Nearby mountains, specifically the Goda Mountains, provide a cooler highland contrast to the coastal heat. Geography K8 — ancient trade routes and historical ports."
